# 9. TMDB TITLE LOGO INTEGRATION

TMDB is exclusively for retrieving transparent anime title logos.

Official documentation:

https://developer.themoviedb.org/docs/getting-started

Do not use TMDB for:
- Anime metadata
- Descriptions
- Ratings
- Genres
- Episodes
- Season information
- Search results displayed to users
- Streaming information
- Posters
- Banners

Use it only to retrieve transparent anime title logos.

### TMDB workflow

Step 1: Obtain the anime title and release year from Hoshika.

Step 2: Search for the corresponding TV series using TMDB TV search.

Step 3: Compare:
- English title
- Original title
- Alternative title, when available
- Release year
- Original language

Step 4: Verify the result matches the Hoshika anime.

Step 5: Obtain the TMDB TV ID.

Step 6: Request TV images and inspect the `logos` collection.

Step 7: Select the most suitable transparent logo.

### Image endpoint

Use the official TMDB TV images endpoint:

`/tv/{tv_id}/images`

Use supported image-language filters.

Prioritize:
1. English logo
2. Japanese logo
3. Language-neutral logo
4. Other suitable logo only if necessary

### Image URL

Use the TMDB image CDN:

`https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/{file_path}`

Use original resolution when appropriate.

### Logo validation

- Prefer PNG with transparency.
- Prefer large-resolution artwork.
- Preserve aspect ratio.
- Do not stretch.
- Avoid logos with excessive empty space when a better version exists.
- Reject unrelated artwork.
- Never display a poster as a title logo.

### TMDB match validation

Do not blindly accept the first search result.

Use title and year matching to prevent different anime adaptations or similarly named series from receiving the wrong logo.

When confidence is insufficient, try alternative Hoshika title fields.

If still uncertain, continue to Fanart.tv.

