# 10. FANART.TV TITLE LOGO FALLBACK

Official documentation:

https://api.fanart.tv/

Fanart.tv is the secondary logo provider.

Only call it when:
- TMDB has no suitable logo.
- TMDB returns no logos.
- The matching TV entry has no usable logo.
- The logo URL is invalid or unavailable.

Use the corresponding TMDB TV ID as the lookup reference, following Fanart.tv documentation.

Use the supported TV logo artwork collection, especially `hdtvlogo`.

### Selection priority

1. English logo
2. Japanese logo
3. Language-neutral logo
4. Other suitable logo

Check image validity and transparency where possible.

Do not replace a valid TMDB logo with a lower-quality Fanart logo.

### Fallback sequence

    Hoshika anime title
          |
          v
    TMDB search
          |
          v
    Verify matching TV series
          |
          v
    TMDB logos
          |
       Found?
       /    \
     Yes     No
      |       |
      v       v
    Display  Fanart.tv
             |
          Logo found?
           /     \
         Yes      No
          |        |
          v        v
       Display   Text title

### Final fallback

If neither TMDB nor Fanart has a valid logo:
- Display the English anime title.
- If English title is unavailable, display the preferred Hoshika title.
- Use clean white typography.
- Do not show an empty image.
- Do not show a broken image placeholder.

### Logo cache

Store:
- Hoshika ID
- TMDB TV ID
- Logo provider
- Logo URL
- Logo language
- Width
- Height
- Last updated
- Validation status

Cache the selected logo locally.

Do not perform logo searches every time a user opens anime details.

Use reasonable cache expiration and allow refreshing missing or invalid artwork.

### API security

TMDB API credentials and Fanart.tv API keys must remain on the backend.

Never hardcode these credentials in the APK.

Use the existing AniScroll backend as the secure proxy.

